# Normalize text files to LF in the repository itself. This does not force
# a particular line ending in anyone's working copy — `eol=lf` only pins
# what gets stored in the blob and what a fresh `git clone` checks out with
# on a platform that has no other opinion; a developer's own core.autocrlf
# still governs conversion on checkout/checkin as usual. Without this file,
# git falls back to core.autocrlf alone, which is how this repo ended up
# with tracked files stored with CRLF line endings (see README/CLAUDE.md's
# Windows dev-server notes) even though every generated page and template
# is authored assuming LF.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Fonts and images: binary, never diffed or line-ending-converted.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.webp binary
*.ico binary
*.woff2 binary
*.woff binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
